- Keep UI text sparse and large enough to appear plausible. Avoid dense paragraphs, fake awards, discount language, mortgage-rate claims, unverified statistics, competitor logos, or unreadable microcopy.
The visual must be clearly about this service and should not introduce another brand, service, or category.
Family intent: Keep FairLend's two-sided business clear, but make Build Financing the dominant path and Investor Platform the secondary path.
Business goal: Clarify FairLend as brokerage and investment company while optimizing for the builder/developer segment..
Scene: A premium FairLend desktop hero mockup with one large left headline and two action panels below: a dominant build-financing project-review panel with progress dots and coral CTA, plus a quieter investor-platform panel. On the right, a realistic Canadian multifamily property fades from blueprint sketch to completed structure, with a brokerage license card tucked near the image..
Focus: Segment clarity without splitting the page into equal competing heroes..
Decision being supported: Can the hero serve both borrowers and investors while clearly prioritizing the conversion-critical builder flow?.
Include: single desktop website hero mockup, two path panels with build financing dominant, investor platform secondary cue, project review stepper, brokerage license proof, blueprint-to-building transition, deep green and coral FairLend palette.
Constraints: do not create a two-page collage; build path must be visually primary; investor path should not steal the main CTA; keep text sparse; use short labels, UI placeholder blocks, or visual markers only when needed; keep the service moment recognizable.
